IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coa5-derivative-claims`
IMPORT `coa-proc-derivative-claims`

-- coa-proc-derivative-claims-tests.l4: tests for coa-proc-derivative-claims.l4 (Companies Act 2006, ss 260 to 264).
-- Every expected outcome is written from the text of the section named beside it, before the run, and never copied from the output.
-- A #TRACE prints FULFILLED, a BREACH or a still-open obligation (RESIDUAL) and no assertion line, so the expected outcome sits on the
-- `-- EXPECT` line directly above each trace and is read against the Result block by expect_check.py.
-- The text gives no time limit anywhere in ss 261 to 264, so no trace has a last day: an event on day 3 and the same event on day 1000 are alike,
-- and a duty or power not yet used stays open (RESIDUAL) however long the trace waits.

§ `Tests for the derivative claims procedure`

§§ `Assertions: the helpers`

-- s 261(4): the court is hearing the application, so the three courses are open to it.
#ASSERT `s 261(4) the court is hearing the application and each of its three courses is open` TRUE
-- s 261(4): the court is not hearing the application, so "on hearing" does not arise.
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 261(4) the court is hearing the application and each of its three courses is open` FALSE))
-- s 262(5): the court is hearing the application, so the three courses are open to it.
#ASSERT `s 262(5) the court is hearing the application and each of its three courses is open` TRUE
-- s 262(5): the court is not hearing the application, so "on hearing" does not arise.
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 262(5) the court is hearing the application and each of its three courses is open` FALSE))
-- s 264(5): the court is hearing the application, so the three courses are open to it.
#ASSERT `s 264(5) the court is hearing the application and each of its three courses is open` TRUE
-- s 264(5): the court is not hearing the application, so "on hearing" does not arise.
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 264(5) the court is hearing the application and each of its three courses is open` FALSE))
-- s 263(2)(a): the court is satisfied that a person acting in accordance with s 172 would not seek to continue the claim.
#ASSERT `s 263(1)-(2) permission (or leave) must be refused on an application under section 261 or 262` (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 263(2)(b): the act or omission is yet to occur and has been authorised by the company.
#ASSERT `s 263(1)-(2) permission (or leave) must be refused on an application under section 261 or 262` (`s 263(2)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur`) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 263(2)(c)(i): the act or omission has already occurred and was authorised before it occurred.
#ASSERT `s 263(1)-(2) permission (or leave) must be refused on an application under section 261 or 262` (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- s 263(2)(c)(ii): the act or omission has already occurred and has been ratified since it occurred.
#ASSERT `s 263(1)-(2) permission (or leave) must be refused on an application under section 261 or 262` (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- s 263(2): the court is satisfied of none of the matters, so permission need not be refused.
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 263(1)-(2) permission (or leave) must be refused on an application under section 261 or 262` (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- s 263(2)(c)(i) is for an act or omission that has already occurred: for one yet to occur, only (b) counts.
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 263(1)-(2) permission (or leave) must be refused on an application under section 261 or 262` (`s 263(2)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur`) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
-- s 263(2)(b) is for an act or omission that is yet to occur: for one that has already occurred, only (a) and (c) count.
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 263(1)-(2) permission (or leave) must be refused on an application under section 261 or 262` (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))

§§ `Traces: s 261, the member who brings a derivative claim`

-- s 261(1): a member brings a derivative claim under the Chapter and applies for permission on day 3.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 261(1) the member's step of applying for permission to continue the derivative claim` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the member who brings the derivative claim` DOES `s 261(1) the member applies to the court for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) to continue the derivative claim` AT 3

-- s 261(1): the member applies on day 1000: the text gives no time, so a late application is as good as an early one.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 261(1) the member's step of applying for permission to continue the derivative claim` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the member who brings the derivative claim` DOES `s 261(1) the member applies to the court for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) to continue the derivative claim` AT 1000

-- s 261(1): the member has not applied by day 30: the text states no time and no consequence, so the duty stays owed.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 261(1) the member's step of applying for permission to continue the derivative claim` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 261(1): no derivative claim is brought under this Chapter, so s 261(1) puts no duty on anyone.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 261(1) the member's step of applying for permission to continue the derivative claim` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 261(2)(a): the application and the evidence disclose no prima facie case; the court dismisses the application on day 5.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 261(2)(a) the court's step of dismissing an application that discloses no prima facie case` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 261(2)(a) the court dismisses the application` AT 5

-- s 261(2)(a): no prima facie case appears and the court has not dismissed by day 30: the duty stays owed, with no clock.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 261(2)(a) the court's step of dismissing an application that discloses no prima facie case` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 261(2)(a): a prima facie case is disclosed, so the court has no duty to dismiss under s 261(2).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 261(2)(a) the court's step of dismissing an application that discloses no prima facie case` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 261(2)(b): the court has dismissed the application and makes a consequential order on day 6.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 261(2)(b) the court's power to make a consequential order after a dismissal` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 261(2)(b) the court makes a consequential order` AT 6

-- s 261(2)(b): a prima facie case is disclosed, so there is no dismissal and no power to make a consequential order.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 261(2)(b) the court's power to make a consequential order after a dismissal` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 261(3)(a): the application is not dismissed under s 261(2); the court gives directions as to the evidence on day 7.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 261(3)(a) the court's power to give directions as to the evidence to be provided by the company` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 261(3)(a) the court gives directions as to the evidence to be provided by the company` AT 7

-- s 261(3)(a): the application is not dismissed and the court has given no directions by day 30: the power stays open, with no clock.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 261(3)(a) the court's power to give directions as to the evidence to be provided by the company` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 261(3)(a): the application is dismissed under s 261(2), so s 261(3) gives the court no power to give directions.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 261(3)(a) the court's power to give directions as to the evidence to be provided by the company` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 261(3)(b): the application is not dismissed; the court adjourns the proceedings to enable the evidence to be obtained, on day 8.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 261(3)(b) the court's power to adjourn the proceedings to enable the evidence to be obtained` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 261(3)(b) the court adjourns the proceedings to enable the evidence to be obtained` AT 8

-- s 261(3)(b): the application is dismissed under s 261(2), so s 261(3) gives the court no power to adjourn.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 261(3)(b) the court's power to adjourn the proceedings to enable the evidence to be obtained` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 261(4)(a): on hearing, nothing in s 263(2) requires refusal; the court gives permission on day 9.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 261(4) the court's step on hearing the application` TRUE (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 261(4)(a) the court gives permission (or leave) to continue the claim on such terms as it thinks fit` AT 9

-- s 261(4)(b): on hearing, nothing in s 263(2) requires refusal; the court refuses permission and dismisses the claim on day 9.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 261(4) the court's step on hearing the application` TRUE (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 261(4)(b) the court refuses permission (or leave) and dismisses the claim` AT 9

-- s 261(4)(c): on hearing, nothing in s 263(2) requires refusal; the court adjourns the proceedings and gives directions on day 9.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 261(4) the court's step on hearing the application` TRUE (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 261(4)(c) the court adjourns the proceedings on the application and gives such directions as it thinks fit` AT 9

-- s 261(4): the court is hearing the application and has taken none of the three courses by day 30: the power stays open, with no clock.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 261(4) the court's step on hearing the application` TRUE (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 261(4): the court is not hearing the application, so "on hearing" gives it no course.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 261(4) the court's step on hearing the application` FALSE (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 263(2)(a): the court is satisfied that a person acting in accordance with s 172 would not seek to continue the claim; the court refuses on day 9.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 261(4) the court's step on hearing the application` TRUE (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 261(4)(b) the court refuses permission (or leave) and dismisses the claim` AT 9

-- s 263(2)(a): the same, and the court has not refused by day 30: the duty to refuse stays owed.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 261(4) the court's step on hearing the application` TRUE (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 263(2)(b): the act or omission is yet to occur and has been authorised by the company; the court refuses on day 9.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 261(4) the court's step on hearing the application` TRUE (`s 263(2)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur`) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 261(4)(b) the court refuses permission (or leave) and dismisses the claim` AT 9

-- s 263(2): the court is satisfied under (a) and adjourns instead of refusing: adjourning is not offered once the court is satisfied, so the duty to refuse stays owed (see the FORK on the rule).
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 261(4) the court's step on hearing the application` TRUE (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 261(4)(c) the court adjourns the proceedings on the application and gives such directions as it thinks fit` AT 9

-- s 263(2): the act or omission is yet to occur and the only matter the court is satisfied of counts only for an act already occurred ((c)(i)): nothing requires refusal, so the court may give permission on day 9.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 261(4) the court's step on hearing the application` TRUE (`s 263(2)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur`) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 261(4)(a) the court gives permission (or leave) to continue the claim on such terms as it thinks fit` AT 9

-- s 263(2): the court is satisfied under (a) and nonetheless gives permission on day 9: permission must be refused, so this is a breach.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 263(2) the court's bar on giving permission (or leave) on an application under section 261` TRUE (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 261(4)(a) the court gives permission (or leave) to continue the claim on such terms as it thinks fit` AT 9

-- s 263(2): the court is satisfied under (a) and has not given permission by day 30: the bar stays open, with no clock.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 263(2) the court's bar on giving permission (or leave) on an application under section 261` TRUE (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 263(2): the court is satisfied of none of the matters, so there is no bar and giving permission on day 9 breaches nothing.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 263(2) the court's bar on giving permission (or leave) on an application under section 261` TRUE (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 261(4)(a) the court gives permission (or leave) to continue the claim on such terms as it thinks fit` AT 9

§§ `Traces: s 262, a member continuing a claim begun by the company`

-- s 262(2): the company has brought a claim that could be pursued as a derivative claim, and all three grounds are made out; the member applies on day 3.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 262(2) the member's power to apply for permission to continue the company's claim as a derivative claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the member who applies to continue the company's claim` DOES `s 262(2) the member applies to the court for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) to continue the claim as a derivative claim` AT 3

-- s 262(2): the manner in which the company commenced or continued the claim is not an abuse of process, so the grounds are not made out and the member has no power to apply.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 262(2) the member's power to apply for permission to continue the company's claim as a derivative claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 262(3)(a): no prima facie case appears; the court dismisses the application on day 5.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 262(3)(a) the court's step of dismissing an application that discloses no prima facie case` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 262(3)(a) the court dismisses the application` AT 5

-- s 262(5)(a): on hearing, nothing in s 263(2) requires refusal; the court gives permission to continue the claim as a derivative claim on day 9.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 262(5) the court's step on hearing the application` TRUE (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 262(5)(a) the court gives permission (or leave) to continue the claim as a derivative claim on such terms as it thinks fit` AT 9

-- s 263(2)(a) applies to an application under s 262: the court is satisfied that a person acting in accordance with s 172 would not seek to continue the claim; it refuses on day 9.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 262(5) the court's step on hearing the application` TRUE (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 262(5)(b) the court refuses permission (or leave) and dismisses the application` AT 9

-- s 263(2): on an application under s 262 the court is satisfied under (a) and gives permission on day 9: a breach.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 263(2) the court's bar on giving permission (or leave) on an application under section 262` TRUE (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 262(5)(a) the court gives permission (or leave) to continue the claim as a derivative claim on such terms as it thinks fit` AT 9

-- s 262(3)(a): a prima facie case is disclosed, so the court has no duty to dismiss under s 262(3).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 262(3)(a) the court's step of dismissing an application that discloses no prima facie case` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 262(3)(b): the court has dismissed the application and makes a consequential order on day 6.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 262(3)(b) the court's power to make a consequential order after a dismissal` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 262(3)(b) the court makes a consequential order` AT 6

-- s 262(3)(b): a prima facie case is disclosed, so there is no dismissal and no power to make a consequential order.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 262(3)(b) the court's power to make a consequential order after a dismissal` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 262(4)(a): the application is not dismissed under s 262(3); the court gives directions as to the evidence on day 7.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 262(4)(a) the court's power to give directions as to the evidence to be provided by the company` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 262(4)(a) the court gives directions as to the evidence to be provided by the company` AT 7

-- s 262(4)(a): the application is dismissed under s 262(3), so s 262(4) gives the court no power to give directions.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 262(4)(a) the court's power to give directions as to the evidence to be provided by the company` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 262(4)(b): the application is not dismissed; the court adjourns the proceedings to enable the evidence to be obtained, on day 8.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 262(4)(b) the court's power to adjourn the proceedings to enable the evidence to be obtained` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 262(4)(b) the court adjourns the proceedings to enable the evidence to be obtained` AT 8

-- s 262(4)(b): the application is dismissed under s 262(3), so s 262(4) gives the court no power to adjourn.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 262(4)(b) the court's power to adjourn the proceedings to enable the evidence to be obtained` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 262(5)(b): on hearing, nothing in s 263(2) requires refusal; the court refuses permission and dismisses the application on day 9.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 262(5) the court's step on hearing the application` TRUE (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 262(5)(b) the court refuses permission (or leave) and dismisses the application` AT 9

-- s 262(5)(c): on hearing, nothing in s 263(2) requires refusal; the court adjourns the proceedings and gives directions on day 9.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 262(5) the court's step on hearing the application` TRUE (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 262(5)(c) the court adjourns the proceedings on the application and gives such directions as it thinks fit` AT 9

-- s 262(5): the court is not hearing the application, so "on hearing" gives it no course.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 262(5) the court's step on hearing the application` FALSE (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 263(2): on an application under s 262 nothing requires refusal, so there is no bar and giving permission on day 9 breaches nothing.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 263(2) the court's bar on giving permission (or leave) on an application under section 262` TRUE (`s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 262(5)(a) the court gives permission (or leave) to continue the claim as a derivative claim on such terms as it thinks fit` AT 9

§§ `Traces: s 264, another member continuing a derivative claim`

-- s 264(2): a member has brought a derivative claim and all three grounds are made out; another member applies on day 3.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 264(2) another member's power to apply for permission to continue the claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 another member of the company` DOES `s 264(2) another member applies to the court for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) to continue the claim` AT 3

-- s 264(1): no member has brought or continued a derivative claim, so s 264 does not apply and no member has the power to apply under it.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 264(2) another member's power to apply for permission to continue the claim` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 264(2): the claimant has not failed to prosecute the claim diligently, so the grounds are not made out and the other member has no power to apply.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 264(2) another member's power to apply for permission to continue the claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 264(3)(a): no prima facie case appears; the court dismisses the application on day 5.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 264(3)(a) the court's step of dismissing an application that discloses no prima facie case` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 264(3)(a) the court dismisses the application` AT 5

-- s 264(5)(a): the court is hearing the application and gives permission to continue the claim on day 9.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 264(5) the court's step on hearing the application` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 264(5)(a) the court gives permission (or leave) to continue the claim on such terms as it thinks fit` AT 9

-- s 264(5)(b): the court refuses permission and dismisses the application on day 9.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 264(5) the court's step on hearing the application` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 264(5)(b) the court refuses permission (or leave) and dismisses the application` AT 9

-- s 264(5): the court is hearing the application and has taken none of the three courses by day 30: the power stays open, with no clock.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 264(5) the court's step on hearing the application` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 264(3)(a): a prima facie case is disclosed, so the court has no duty to dismiss under s 264(3).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 264(3)(a) the court's step of dismissing an application that discloses no prima facie case` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 264(3)(b): the court has dismissed the application and makes a consequential order on day 6.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 264(3)(b) the court's power to make a consequential order after a dismissal` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 264(3)(b) the court makes a consequential order` AT 6

-- s 264(3)(b): a prima facie case is disclosed, so there is no dismissal and no power to make a consequential order.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 264(3)(b) the court's power to make a consequential order after a dismissal` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 264(4)(a): the application is not dismissed under s 264(3); the court gives directions as to the evidence on day 7.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 264(4)(a) the court's power to give directions as to the evidence to be provided by the company` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 264(4)(a) the court gives directions as to the evidence to be provided by the company` AT 7

-- s 264(4)(a): the application is dismissed under s 264(3), so s 264(4) gives the court no power to give directions.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 264(4)(a) the court's power to give directions as to the evidence to be provided by the company` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 264(4)(b): the application is not dismissed; the court adjourns the proceedings to enable the evidence to be obtained, on day 8.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 264(4)(b) the court's power to adjourn the proceedings to enable the evidence to be obtained` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 264(4)(b) the court adjourns the proceedings to enable the evidence to be obtained` AT 8

-- s 264(4)(b): the application is dismissed under s 264(3), so s 264(4) gives the court no power to adjourn.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 264(4)(b) the court's power to adjourn the proceedings to enable the evidence to be obtained` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 264(5)(c): the court is hearing the application and adjourns the proceedings and gives such directions as it thinks fit on day 9.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 264(5) the court's step on hearing the application` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 260-264 the court` DOES `s 264(5)(c) the court adjourns the proceedings on the application and gives such directions as it thinks fit` AT 9

-- s 264(5): the court is not hearing the application, so "on hearing" gives it no course.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 264(5) the court's step on hearing the application` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)


-- READS-DIFFERENTLY-ON-MAIN:
-- No trace in this file differs in class (FULFILLED, BREACH, RESIDUAL) between the unstable build (a50cbd0, 25 November 2026) and main (112):
-- all 60 traces match their EXPECT on both, and all 13 assertions are satisfied on both. The Result block prints differently on main in one trace, with the same class on both:
--   * the s 263(2) bar on an application under s 261, in the trace where the court is satisfied under (a) and has not given permission by day 30 (the open prohibition, RESIDUAL):
--     unstable prints the LEST with its BREACH in parentheses, main without.
